---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

/**
 * The clause that matters most here is "What Stick does not promise": the
 * product is friction, not security, and a buyer who defeats it has not been
 * sold a defective good. It has to stand on its own now that the detailed
 * limitations page is gone — do not weaken it without replacing it.
 *
 * The entity, the governing law and the business address are all in now. A
 * lawyer should still read this page before it does much more work.
 *
 * The address is Noah's own, published knowingly as the interim answer until
 * there is an office — see the note on `businessAddress` in src/config.ts.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Terms of sale | Stick"
  description="What you agree to when you buy a Stick: pre-order terms, what the product does and does not promise, and your rights."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-14 md:pt-24">
    <h1 class="headline text-hero">Terms of sale</h1>
    <div class="mt-9 space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p>
        These are the terms you agree to when you buy a Stick from
        {' '}{site.legalEntity}. We've tried to write them in plain English, because
        terms nobody reads protect nobody.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[15px]">Last updated {site.policyUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-16">
    <div class="space-y-12">
      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          What you're buying
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          One Stick, a USB-C key, and a licence to use the Stick app on any Mac
          or Windows PC you own. {site.price} plus shipping, charged once. There
          is no subscription and no recurring charge of any kind.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The Mac app requires {site.minMacOS}, and runs on both Apple Silicon
          and Intel Macs from a single download. The Windows app requires{' '}
          {site.minWindows}, on {site.windowsArchitectures}. Both are included
          in the price and neither is charged for separately. On a system older
          than either, Stick will not run, and we'd rather you knew before
          paying than after.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          This is a pre-order
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You are charged when you order, before the product ships. Most orders
          ship in {site.shipWindow}, with a limited first batch in
          {' '}{site.earlyShipWindow}. Ordering early may put you in that batch;
          it is not a guarantee that it will.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          If either date moves, we will email you and tell you. At that point you
          can cancel for a full refund, or wait. Your choice, and asking costs
          you nothing. We will not quietly hold your money against an indefinite
          date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          What Stick does not promise
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink"
            >Stick is friction, not security.</strong
          > It is designed to defeat an impulse, not a determined person with administrator
          rights on their own computer. On a machine you control, it can be circumvented,
          and you should buy it assuming that it can.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Specifically: we do not warrant that Stick will prevent you or anyone
          else from accessing any particular website or application, that a
          session cannot be ended without the key, or that it will produce any
          outcome in your habits, productivity or wellbeing. Successfully getting
          around Stick is not a defect.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Stick is a tool for limiting your own computer. It is not a monitoring
          or parental-control product, and it is not sold for supervising anyone
          else's device.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          If it's faulty, and if you change your mind
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The key is warranted against manufacturing defects for one year from
          delivery. If it fails, we replace it or refund it and cover postage
          both ways.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Separately, you can cancel any time before your order ships, and you
          have 30 days from delivery to send it back for a refund of the price.
          Full detail is on the{' '}
          <a href="/refunds" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
            >refunds page</a
          >, which also forms part of these terms.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink"
            >None of this reduces your statutory rights.</strong
          > If you're a consumer in the UK, EU or anywhere with mandatory consumer
          protection, those rights apply on top of what's written here and win wherever
          they conflict.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Shipping, duties and tax
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Shipping is charged separately from the {site.price} price, at
          checkout, and the amount depends on where it is going.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Import duties, customs charges and local taxes, where your country
          levies them on arrival, are yours to pay. We can't calculate these for
          every country and we don't collect them on your behalf.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Risk of loss passes to you on delivery. If a parcel is lost in transit,
          that's ours to sort out. Tell us and we will.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Using the software
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You get a personal, non-exclusive licence to run the Stick app on any
          Mac or Windows PC you own, for as long as you like. Updates are included at no cost. You
          own the physical key outright and can sell it or give it away; the
          licence goes with it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You may not redistribute or resell the software on its own. Beyond
          that, we're not going to tell you what to do with software running on
          your own machine.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Payment
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Payment is handled by Shopify. We never see your full card number. What
          we hold and why is set out in the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
            >privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          We may cancel and refund an order if it was priced in error, if we
          can't ship to your address, or if we suspect fraud. If we do, you get
          your money back in full.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Liability
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          To the extent the law allows, our total liability to you is limited to
          what you paid for your Stick. We're not liable for indirect or
          consequential losses: missed work, lost data, or anything you couldn't
          reach while a session was running.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Nothing here limits liability for death or personal injury caused by
          negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that can't lawfully be
          limited.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Which law applies
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          {site.legalEntity} is a {site.jurisdiction} limited liability
          company, and these terms are governed by the laws of the State of{' '}
          {site.jurisdiction}. Our business address is{' '}
          {site.businessAddress.join(', ')}.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          If you are a consumer, this does not take away the protection of the
          mandatory consumer law of the country you live in, and it does not
          stop you bringing a claim in your local courts where that law gives
          you the right to. Those rights come first.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Changes, and getting in touch
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The terms that apply to your order are the ones published when you
          ordered. Changes are not retroactive.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Questions, cancellations, faults, anything at all. Email{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{site.supportEmail}</a
          >. We answer {site.unlockResponseTime}.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
